{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To solve the problem, we need to determine the five positive integers that satisfy the given conditions: the average (mean) is 5, the median is 5, and the only mode is 8. Let's denote the five integers by \\(a, b, c, d, e\\) in non-decreasing order, i.e., \\(a \\leq b \\leq c \\leq d \\leq e\\).\n\n### Step 1: Use the mean condition\nThe average of the five integers is 5. Therefore, the sum of the integers is:\n\\[\na + b + c + d + e = 5 \\times 5 = 25\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Use the median condition\nThe median of the five integers is 5. Since the integers are in non-decreasing order, the median \\(c\\) is:\n\\[\nc = 5\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Use the mode condition\nThe only mode is 8. This means that 8 appears more frequently than any other integer in the set. Since there are five integers, and 8 must appear at least twice (to be the mode), and no other integer can appear more than once, the integers must be:\n\\[\na, b, 5, 8, 8\n\\]\n\n### Step 4: Substitute and solve for the remaining integers\nWe know:\n\\[\na + b + 5 + 8 + 8 = 25\n\\]\nSimplify the equation:\n\\[\na + b + 21 = 25\n\\]\nSubtract 21 from both sides:\n\\[\na + b = 4\n\\]\n\n","prefix_end":1097,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":false,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,11625,279,3491,11,582,1184,311,8253,279,4236,6785,25780,429,26553,279,2661,4682,25,279,5461,320,14287,8,374,220,20,11,279,22553,374,220,20,11,323,279,1172,3856,374,220,23,13,6771,594,78064,279,4236,25780,553,17767,64,11,293,11,272,11,294,11,384,57758,304,2477,6810,75462,1973,11,600,1734,2572,17767,64,1124,273,80,293,1124,273,80,272,1124,273,80,294,1124,273,80,384,59,3593,14374,14822,220,16,25,5443,279,3076,2971,198,785,5461,315,279,4236,25780,374,220,20,13,15277,11,279,2629,315,279,25780,374,510,59,9640,64,488,293,488,272,488,294,488,384,284,220,20,1124,15136,220,20,284,220,17,20,198,59,2533,14374,14822,220,17,25,5443,279